  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 4,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.648,
            0.047,
            0.846,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Working with Fractions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the previous day. How many hours after 10 pm will the moon set on Thursday?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.13,
            0.691,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Multiply and then convert it into a mixed fraction:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.155,
            0.317,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 \\times \\frac { 3 } { 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (b) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 \\times { \\frac { 1 } { 3 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (c) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 9 } { 7 } \\times 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (d) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 3 } { 1 1 } \\times 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.308,
            0.848,
            0.366
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So far, we have learnt multiplication of a whole number with a fraction, and a fraction with a whole number. What happens when both numbers in the multiplication are fractions?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.383,
            0.479,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Multiplying Two Fractions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.42,
            0.846,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know, that Aaron’s pet tortoise can walk only "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " km in 1 hour. How far can it walk in half an hour?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.47,
            0.605,
            0.527
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Following our approach of using multiplication to solve such problems, we have,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.528,
            0.56,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Distance covered in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{2} \\text { hour } = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{4}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " km."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.576,
            0.373,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Finding the product:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.614,
            0.458,
            0.843,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.614,
                0.458,
                0.843,
                0.597
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_table_10.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Hour</td><td>Distance</td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">1</td><td rowspan=\"2\">14</td></tr><tr></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">12</td><td rowspan=\"2\">?</td></tr><tr></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.602,
            0.499,
            0.635
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Distance covered in 1 "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{h0ur} = \\frac{1}{4} \\mathrm{km}."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.632,
            0.846,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, the distance covered in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " an hour is the length we get by dividing "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " into 2 equal parts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.692,
            0.846,
            0.73
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To find this, it is useful to represent fractions using the unit square to stand for a “whole”."
            }
          ]
        },
